          "date": "2026-11-10 01:20:57.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21132 build: drop redundant kswapd checks",
        "message": "LU-21132 build: drop redundant kswapd checks\n\nLinux commit v7.3-rc5-546-g27517f701ff3 (\"mm: replace PF_KSWAPD flag\nwith kthread_func() check\") removed PF_KSWAPD, breaking builds in\nosd_object_delete() and qsd_start_reint_thread().\n\nDrop the PF_KSWAPD checks instead of replacing them with\ncurrent_is_kswapd().  kswapd and direct reclaim both run with\nPF_MEMALLOC set, so PF_KSWAPD was only ever set when PF_MEMALLOC was\ntoo.  The one exception is a softirq running on kswapd's stack, where\nPF_MEMALLOC is masked.  However, these functions can sleep and so are\nnever called from softirq context.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chell Laszlo <pumpkinbiscuit@proton.me>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-fable-5-1\nChange-Id: I329d0688a846661eb8f38a5da2bc02dbadc42174\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
